cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
title: "SECL: Self-Calibrating Language Models via Test-Time Discriminative Distillation"
abstract: >-
  SECL is a test-time training (TTT) pipeline that calibrates large language
  models without labels, distilling the better-calibrated normalized P(True)
  discriminative signal into verbalized confidence via lightweight LoRA updates
  gated by Page-Hinkley entropy change detection.
